{"hw":"ἄπορος","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἄπορος</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἄπορος</span>, <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ον</span>, first in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> </span> and <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> </span> (v.infr.), <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">without passage, having no way in, out,</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">through</b>: hence, </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">I</span> of places, <b class=\"lex-tr\">impassable,</b> <span class=\"gk\">πέλαγος, π<span class=\"lex-itype gk\">ηλός</span>,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ti.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">25d</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Criti.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">108e</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ὁδός, ὀρη,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">An.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.4.4</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.5.18</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> of states or circumstances, <b class=\"lex-tr\">impracticable, difficult,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hdt.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">5.3</span> </span>, etc.; <span class=\"gk\">ἄ. ἀλγηδών, πάθη,</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">513</span> </span> (lyr.), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">854</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τἄπορον ἔτος</span> ib.<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cit